WEBVTT

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:04.190
In this place so unreal

00:00:03.900 --> 00:00:07.820
I wait for dawn to come

00:00:07.530 --> 00:00:12.950
Farther and farther, like the sky I saw that day

00:00:15.160 --> 00:00:19.250
What a joke this hope is

00:00:18.920 --> 00:00:22.750
I acted as if I had forgotten

00:00:22.500 --> 00:00:28.260
Farther and farther, like the dream I saw that day

00:00:29.470 --> 00:00:34.140
I just want to know the meaning of it

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:37.310
Within this scattered time

00:00:37.020 --> 00:00:41.150
Along with the breath of ours

00:00:41.150 --> 00:00:45.070
And of this pain that never goes away

00:00:44.770 --> 00:00:48.610
Even though the roaring of the sea muffles the voices

00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:52.530
Darkness engulfs everything ahead

00:00:52.200 --> 00:00:56.540
The light that passes through our fragile hearts

00:00:56.450 --> 00:00:59.960
Won't go away

00:00:59.750 --> 00:01:03.790
We only relied on our compass

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.920
We believed you

00:01:07.670 --> 00:01:14.760
While we stand here

00:01:14.470 --> 00:01:19.930
We're searching for the unseen future

00:01:22.900 --> 00:01:29.860
Zipang

00:01:35.030 --> 00:01:38.490
the SDF Navy's newest AEGIS class vessel, Mirai,

00:01:38.490 --> 00:01:40.870
sets off from the Yokosuka Base.

00:01:41.370 --> 00:01:44.000
However, just as they entered the Pacific Ocean,

00:01:44.290 --> 00:01:47.330
Mirai was faced with abnormal atmospheric conditions.

00:01:47.330 --> 00:01:50.750
She was then thrown back to 1942, June 4th,

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:53.050
into the Battle of Midway.

00:01:54.380 --> 00:01:57.300
Caught in the midst of an ongoing war,

00:01:57.300 --> 00:02:03.470
what should the 240 SDF members of the Mirai do in this era?

00:02:04.390 --> 00:02:07.980
We have yet to find the answer.

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:29.920
The Pursuer

00:02:32.420 --> 00:02:35.550
Black market prices have been soaring the past few days?!

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:32.590
Great Nippon
Imperial Army
25th General
Headquarters

00:02:32.540 --> 00:02:32.590
Singapore
Signal Corps

00:02:32.550 --> 00:02:35.550
Great Nippon
Imperial Army
25th General
Headquarters

00:02:35.550 --> 00:02:37.510
Now that's good to hear!

00:02:37.510 --> 00:02:39.680
The black market running low on food supplies?

00:02:39.680 --> 00:02:42.680
That's proof that the army is doing a good job managing this country!

00:02:43.680 --> 00:02:45.140
What?

00:02:45.850 --> 00:02:48.390
You say someone is buying up all the food supplies?

00:02:49.560 --> 00:02:52.980
Maybe it's some greedy merchant trying to jack up the prices?

00:02:54.110 --> 00:02:55.360
Doesn't seem like it?

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.280
A suspiciously large amount of military notes in circulation?!

00:02:58.280 --> 00:03:00.450
Half a year since occupation,

00:03:00.450 --> 00:03:04.620
rumors of a big scale black market leakage started a few days back.

00:03:04.620 --> 00:03:06.870
It's probably the work of the Chinese.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:08.660
We've not seen the last of it yet.

00:03:08.790 --> 00:03:12.500
Power alone isn't enough to win the people's support.

00:03:12.500 --> 00:03:15.340
The army's having a tough time, too.

00:03:16.170 --> 00:03:19.760
Well, inform me if you have news of suspicious vessels.

00:03:20.800 --> 00:03:23.260
An espionage... you say?

00:03:23.260 --> 00:03:26.350
The Navy isn't having it any easier, I must say.

00:03:26.390 --> 00:03:28.520
Yes, it's the same.

00:03:35.060 --> 00:03:37.610
Have you gotten hold of any information on those two?

00:03:37.610 --> 00:03:40.990
Yes. I've enlisted the help of the police force in the search for them.

00:03:40.990 --> 00:03:43.610
They were last spotted in the Japanese District.

00:03:44.700 --> 00:03:47.030
- Remember they aren't amateurs.
- Yes.

00:03:47.030 --> 00:03:49.790
Not just the Japanese district, but the Chinese District,

00:03:49.790 --> 00:03:51.580
and the Malay District must be covered as well.

00:03:52.620 --> 00:03:54.040
Yes, Sir.

00:03:58.130 --> 00:04:00.300
Black market prices have been on the rise recently.

00:04:00.300 --> 00:04:03.510
- Someone's hoarding goods?
- It's for rice and other foods.

00:04:03.510 --> 00:04:05.140
What does that mean?

00:04:05.340 --> 00:04:09.100
Information can be found in the least expected of places.

00:04:09.470 --> 00:04:11.520
- Found anything on your side?
- Yes!

00:04:11.520 --> 00:04:14.230
I've been talking to employees working at sailor catered bars.

00:04:14.230 --> 00:04:16.900
There've been complaints of the military overworking people.

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:19.400
Mostly from sailors and port officers.

00:04:19.570 --> 00:04:21.530
Oh? Anymore?

00:04:21.530 --> 00:04:23.950
It's something about an emergency tanker,

00:04:23.950 --> 00:04:26.410
to depart in five days right after docking.

00:04:26.410 --> 00:04:29.120
Seems they just finished loading the gas this morning.

00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:32.040
We're at war. It's not an uncommon thing.

00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:35.370
What's more, on top of 3500 kiloliters of diesel,

00:04:35.370 --> 00:04:38.540
they're gonna be stocking up on a large quantity of food, too.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:42.380
There might be some top secret operation we don't know of.

00:04:42.380 --> 00:04:44.800
The Shipping Management Association! Hurry!

00:04:44.800 --> 00:04:46.220
Yes!

00:04:48.390 --> 00:04:50.390
Shipping Management Association
Singapore Branch

00:04:54.310 --> 00:04:57.940
It is all classified information. I'm ordered not to speak of it.

00:05:00.320 --> 00:05:04.070
Why you! We are also soldiers from the same Imperial Navy!

00:05:04.400 --> 00:05:08.830
By the way, the anti-Japanese rebel arrested yesterday...

00:05:08.830 --> 00:05:11.080
...divulged a piece of alarming news.

00:05:11.410 --> 00:05:15.830
They've planted some bombs in a tanker acquired by the military.

00:05:15.830 --> 00:05:17.330
Did you say bombs?!

00:05:17.420 --> 00:05:19.000
The rebel committed suicide,

00:05:19.000 --> 00:05:20.920
so we couldn't get the ship's name out of him.

00:05:20.920 --> 00:05:23.760
All the tankers under the Navy have been thoroughly checked.

00:05:23.760 --> 00:05:26.470
Nothing was found on the army's ships, either.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:28.680
What's left are the civilian ships.

00:05:30.430 --> 00:05:33.060
It's the <i>Toshin Maru</i> from Toyo Steamships!

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:35.100
The <i>Toshin Maru</i>, huh?

00:05:35.480 --> 00:05:36.770
Tomorrow at 10 pm,

00:05:36.770 --> 00:05:39.440
it's scheduled for departure from Pier 3 of the Shonan Port!

00:05:39.440 --> 00:05:41.820
Crew including captain is 25 men!

00:05:43.480 --> 00:05:46.070
Thanks for your help. Please leave it to us.

00:05:47.070 --> 00:05:50.870
By the way, the people who came for this tanker's acquisition,

00:05:50.870 --> 00:05:54.950
was a fair-skinned Navy Lieutenant and a sturdy man in a jacket?

00:05:58.000 --> 00:06:00.250
- Keep watch at Pier 3.
- Yes!

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:03.590
Don't lose them this time! Report any changes at once!

00:06:03.590 --> 00:06:05.510
Yes! Right away!

00:06:07.130 --> 00:06:08.890
Lieutenant Kusaka.

00:06:09.470 --> 00:06:11.800
What're you doing here at Shonan Port?

00:06:16.310 --> 00:06:18.060
Any news from the Executive Officer?

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:19.600
No, none at all.

00:06:19.690 --> 00:06:22.150
If there are any news, I'll report to you right away.

00:06:24.110 --> 00:06:25.820
No news from them...

00:06:25.820 --> 00:06:28.030
...should be a sign that all is proceeding smoothly.

00:06:28.240 --> 00:06:30.110
Any other new findings?

00:06:30.360 --> 00:06:33.370
Besides the canoe with the fishermen this morning,

00:06:33.370 --> 00:06:35.120
nothing else unusual happened.

00:06:35.330 --> 00:06:38.330
It might be a coastal watcher by the Allied forces.

00:06:38.330 --> 00:06:40.210
We should tighten our security level.

00:06:40.210 --> 00:06:42.880
I think they're nothing more than a fisherman and his son.

00:06:42.880 --> 00:06:45.500
We can't possibly kill them both just because they saw us?

00:06:45.500 --> 00:06:47.210
And we can't tell them not to see us.

00:06:47.210 --> 00:06:51.140
Fisherman or not, the fact remains that this ship was discovered.

00:06:51.340 --> 00:06:53.600
We have... three days.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:57.310
Besides believing in our XO, there's nothing we can do.

00:07:16.290 --> 00:07:19.040
In this war, some things will change for the Japanese,

00:07:19.040 --> 00:07:21.120
and some will not.

00:07:21.120 --> 00:07:23.080
It'll be good to watch them closely.

00:07:26.130 --> 00:07:29.300
We've no idea what a real war is like.

00:07:29.920 --> 00:07:32.390
We learnt from school and history books,

00:07:32.390 --> 00:07:34.550
and act like we understand what war is.

00:07:35.220 --> 00:07:39.230
But you have to experience it to really understand.

00:07:41.890 --> 00:07:43.520
Executive Officer,

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:47.690
besides watching Kusaka, there's something I'd like you to do.

00:07:48.070 --> 00:07:53.910
This might become the deciding factor for Mirai's future from now.

00:07:54.200 --> 00:07:59.330
The people living in this era, I want you to watch them closely.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:02.500
Kadomatsu, observe this era closely.

00:08:26.780 --> 00:08:29.530
Toshin Maru

00:08:36.410 --> 00:08:38.620
It's the port laborers!

00:08:38.620 --> 00:08:41.410
They'll start to load the ship with food supplies.

00:08:41.410 --> 00:08:45.170
Lieutenant Tsuda, food supply loading progressing smoothly!

00:08:45.370 --> 00:08:48.130
It should be ready to depart in 7 hours as scheduled!

00:08:48.130 --> 00:08:49.920
Have those two men appeared?

00:08:49.920 --> 00:08:53.220
No, they're nowhere in sight, but we don't have much time.

00:08:53.220 --> 00:08:54.630
I think we should stop them.

00:08:54.720 --> 00:08:56.260
Alright.

00:08:56.260 --> 00:08:58.890
- Let's seize the <i>Toshin Maru</i>!
- Yes!

00:09:04.640 --> 00:09:06.100
I'm very sorry, but...

00:09:06.480 --> 00:09:10.520
I'm not the Navy Officer that you're looking for.

00:09:11.900 --> 00:09:13.940
Lieutenant Kusaka.

00:09:15.910 --> 00:09:20.080
The greeting speech you made earlier on, it was so inspiring!

00:09:20.620 --> 00:09:23.540
Words are not pure information.

00:09:23.870 --> 00:09:26.540
They're interspersed with useless emotion and opinions.

00:09:26.540 --> 00:09:29.790
As a Communications Officer, it is important to remember this point.

00:09:29.790 --> 00:09:33.630
Actions and the final outcome will never betray you.

00:09:33.630 --> 00:09:36.130
It's been a month since the Battle of Midway.

00:09:36.130 --> 00:09:37.840
What exactly happened to you?

00:09:38.180 --> 00:09:40.140
Why do you disguise yourself?

00:09:40.140 --> 00:09:41.850
Why pretend to be someone else?

00:09:42.180 --> 00:09:44.520
You must be hiding something!

00:09:44.520 --> 00:09:46.850
What could be the reason for you to hide your identity?

00:09:49.560 --> 00:09:50.360
Yes!

00:09:50.610 --> 00:09:52.400
Yes! Lieutenant Tsuda?

00:09:52.400 --> 00:09:54.280
Please wait a minute.

00:09:54.280 --> 00:09:56.070
Lieutenant Tsuda.

00:09:56.530 --> 00:09:57.860
I'm busy at the moment!

00:09:57.910 --> 00:10:00.410
It is regarding the unidentified battleship.

00:10:00.410 --> 00:10:01.870
What?

00:10:03.540 --> 00:10:04.950
Yes, Tsuda speaking.

00:10:04.950 --> 00:10:08.420
Information about the mysterious ship just came in.

00:10:08.960 --> 00:10:11.790
We had a call from the Military Police a moment ago.

00:10:11.790 --> 00:10:13.750
At Anambas, a local fisherman...

00:10:13.750 --> 00:10:17.930
...reported seeing a battleship with a Japanese name on it.

00:10:18.260 --> 00:10:23.930
I thought it's strange for our own ship to be hiding in our waters.

00:10:25.770 --> 00:10:28.560
That is just one of our navy's auxiliary vessels.

00:10:28.560 --> 00:10:31.940
They're safe. Thank you for the trouble.

00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:39.240
Halt the seizure of <i>Toshin Maru</i>. We will change our strategy!

00:10:39.240 --> 00:10:40.780
Yes!

00:10:41.620 --> 00:10:43.780
It all links up, Lieutenant Kusaka.

00:10:43.780 --> 00:10:47.200
Please let me see it. I want to see you in action.

00:11:01.970 --> 00:11:03.180
I've seen the port.

00:11:03.640 --> 00:11:04.640
How is it?

00:11:04.720 --> 00:11:07.100
There're a lot of men working there.

00:11:07.100 --> 00:11:08.480
They're carrying a lot of stuff.

00:11:08.480 --> 00:11:11.230
As for military uniformed men, not a single one in sight.

00:11:11.230 --> 00:11:14.190
You've done very well. Here's your reward.

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:17.230
Thank you, sir!

00:11:18.280 --> 00:11:19.650
Alright, what's next?

00:11:19.650 --> 00:11:22.700
That man named Tsuda. Just how much has he found out about us?

00:11:23.570 --> 00:11:25.870
We will know once the tanker sets out.

00:11:26.660 --> 00:11:28.580
Very well.

00:11:49.730 --> 00:11:53.020
Assorted canned items, 9000 cans. 8 tons in all.

00:11:53.100 --> 00:11:57.070
Fresh foods, 6 tons. And 10 tons of Thai rice.

00:11:57.440 --> 00:11:59.740
I was worried about the storage space,

00:11:59.740 --> 00:12:02.030
but it all seems to have worked out fine.

00:12:02.530 --> 00:12:05.070
Hey, the man named Tsuda.

00:12:05.070 --> 00:12:06.700
Do you think he's already on the move?

00:12:06.700 --> 00:12:09.580
I don't know. But it might've been unnecessary concern.

00:12:09.580 --> 00:12:11.460
I sure hope that's the case.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:13.750
I am the Captain of <i>Toshin Maru</i>, Toi.

00:12:17.290 --> 00:12:18.500
Sorry for the trouble.

00:12:18.500 --> 00:12:22.590
We're glad that this ship can contribute in serving our country.

00:12:22.680 --> 00:12:24.680
The loading of supplies is going smoothly.

00:12:24.680 --> 00:12:28.060
We shall depart at 10 PM as scheduled.

00:12:28.060 --> 00:12:32.730
We will be taking anti-submarine measures on route to Anambas,

00:12:32.730 --> 00:12:35.350
and arrive at 10 in the morning as scheduled.

00:12:35.350 --> 00:12:37.060
Do you have any further questions?

00:12:37.060 --> 00:12:39.070
No, that'll do.

00:12:39.230 --> 00:12:41.690
Well then, we will proceed as scheduled.

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:45.490
We still have to prepare for departure, so please excuse us.

00:12:51.370 --> 00:12:54.080
He seems like a good captain to me.

00:12:55.210 --> 00:12:57.170
I think we can rely on him.

00:13:06.180 --> 00:13:09.350
The defeat, according to the history books, is in 3 years.

00:13:10.260 --> 00:13:14.020
I wonder what will become of Teruko of Shonan House then?

00:13:29.950 --> 00:13:33.080
That man there... I didn't see him before the ship departed.

00:13:33.080 --> 00:13:36.000
From the way he walks... he must be a soldier.

00:13:36.000 --> 00:13:39.420
He might be a soldier disguised as the ship's crew.

00:13:39.420 --> 00:13:41.670
I think we should investigate further.

00:13:41.920 --> 00:13:44.720
We must not lead them to Mirai's hiding place.

00:13:44.840 --> 00:13:46.430
I understand.

00:13:46.430 --> 00:13:48.680
12 more hours before we reach Anambas.

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.220
We don't have time to waste.

00:13:50.470 --> 00:13:54.270
Let's split up. I'll go have a talk with Captain Toi himself.

00:13:54.270 --> 00:13:57.390
I will go check up on that man earlier on.

00:14:01.360 --> 00:14:04.320
Making use of that pistol of yours might complicate things.

00:14:04.360 --> 00:14:07.400
And don't try to cover things up by laughing them off.

00:14:13.490 --> 00:14:15.200
Hey.

00:14:17.790 --> 00:14:19.210
What is it?

00:14:19.210 --> 00:14:23.250
Nature calls, you see. Do you know where the toilet on this ship is?

00:14:23.250 --> 00:14:24.460
The toilet's...

00:14:24.630 --> 00:14:26.670
The unfamiliar clothes aside,

00:14:26.670 --> 00:14:29.470
you're not too familiar with this ship either, aren't you?

00:14:42.480 --> 00:14:45.530
I thought so, military uniforms suit you better.

00:14:50.450 --> 00:14:52.410
Lieutenant Takumi Kusaka.

00:14:53.370 --> 00:14:55.990
You've gotten better, Tsuda.

00:14:56.330 --> 00:14:59.000
So you finally remember who I am.

00:14:59.000 --> 00:15:02.710
Admiral Yamamoto will be happy to hear that, too.

00:15:03.710 --> 00:15:05.550
Since it has come to this,

00:15:05.550 --> 00:15:08.380
there's something that I must tell you about.

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:10.130
Huh?

00:15:14.430 --> 00:15:16.470
This is surprising.

00:15:16.470 --> 00:15:19.770
So the whole crew has been replaced.

00:15:25.440 --> 00:15:27.400
Come! Go up!

00:15:33.200 --> 00:15:36.240
A ship... that transcends time?

00:15:36.240 --> 00:15:38.830
Is this some science-fiction tale you've made up?!

00:15:38.830 --> 00:15:40.830
You've always been composed,

00:15:40.830 --> 00:15:43.170
and you loved the Imperial Navy more than anyone else!

00:15:43.210 --> 00:15:46.630
I respected you as a soldier, and regarded you as my ideal!

00:15:46.630 --> 00:15:48.510
No, I believed in you as a person!

00:15:48.840 --> 00:15:52.510
For an ordinary man as myself. The truth of that tale...

00:15:53.510 --> 00:15:57.140
Or even the possibility of something like that happening!

00:15:57.140 --> 00:15:59.220
But there's one thing I do know for sure...

00:15:59.810 --> 00:16:03.600
No one in the upper authorities is going to buy that story of yours!

00:16:07.650 --> 00:16:11.860
So, you're the man who knows the history of what's going to happen?

00:16:13.950 --> 00:16:16.410
What will become of Japan in the future?

00:16:17.910 --> 00:16:21.210
What's the outcome of this war? Answer me now!

00:16:22.960 --> 00:16:24.920
There's no meaning in knowing.

00:16:25.710 --> 00:16:27.130
Why is that?!

00:16:27.130 --> 00:16:28.920
That history is now changing.

00:16:28.920 --> 00:16:30.960
No, we will be changing that history!

00:16:31.260 --> 00:16:34.970
The final outcome of this war, the future of our country...

00:16:34.970 --> 00:16:36.970
...is now right here in our hands!

00:16:38.560 --> 00:16:42.520
Do you not think we have that power, Commander Kadomatsu?

00:16:44.600 --> 00:16:48.230
Why you... Are you planning on playing God?!

00:16:48.440 --> 00:16:50.610
I'm am no God.

00:16:50.610 --> 00:16:52.740
It is humans who can change things!

00:16:53.150 --> 00:16:56.160
Is it a future that must definitely be changed?

00:16:58.120 --> 00:17:02.080
Interesting! How do we change it? What sort of future do you want?!

00:17:02.080 --> 00:17:05.290
I want to conclude this losing battle of ours fast,

00:17:05.290 --> 00:17:08.090
and save as many Japanese people as possible.

00:17:08.960 --> 00:17:12.460
And do you have any reason to stop me from doing so?

00:17:12.460 --> 00:17:15.800
Navy Lieutenant Takumi Kusaka no longer exists.

00:17:15.800 --> 00:17:17.390
That's what you said.

00:17:17.390 --> 00:17:21.600
That is why I allowed you access to the data at Mirai's library!

00:17:22.060 --> 00:17:24.430
For a person of this era to know...

00:17:24.430 --> 00:17:26.600
...the history of tomorrow is extremely painful.

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:29.610
Knowing it would greatly affect your judgment,

00:17:29.610 --> 00:17:31.780
I still let you see the future!

00:17:32.070 --> 00:17:34.900
Because that was the only way you could survive...

00:17:34.900 --> 00:17:36.860
...after knowing so much about us.

00:17:36.990 --> 00:17:41.120
But now, you are telling all this to an Imperial Navy officer?!

00:17:41.120 --> 00:17:45.750
Not a single one of us on board the Mirai wants to alter history!

00:17:46.250 --> 00:17:48.130
Just which side are you on?!

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:51.250
Which side of the world do you live on?!

00:17:54.210 --> 00:17:55.760
I'm on neither side.

00:17:55.760 --> 00:17:57.220
What?!

00:17:57.220 --> 00:18:01.050
If I have to make a choice, I'll say I am Japanese.

00:18:01.180 --> 00:18:05.100
The one who creates history is not God. It's mankind.

00:18:05.230 --> 00:18:07.980
And you are already moving in that direction for that purpose.

00:18:09.350 --> 00:18:10.900
And it's not just the two of us.

00:18:10.900 --> 00:18:15.030
Lieutenant Tsuda, and his 25 subordinates, and most of all,

00:18:15.110 --> 00:18:19.110
this <i>Toshin Maru</i> is moving forward into a new chapter of history.

00:18:19.450 --> 00:18:22.450
Next month, on August 7th,

00:18:22.450 --> 00:18:25.370
a cruel defense battle at Guadalcanal will take place.

00:18:25.370 --> 00:18:28.710
Ichiki's detachment of the army's 1st platoon will be sent there.

00:18:28.710 --> 00:18:32.790
You already know what'll happen to the 916 soldiers sent there.

00:18:33.840 --> 00:18:35.550
You plunged into the dark waters...

00:18:35.550 --> 00:18:38.510
...to rescue me from a sinking seaplane.

00:18:38.680 --> 00:18:42.100
Someone like you will not stand by and watch those men die.

00:18:42.100 --> 00:18:43.810
Because you...

00:18:43.810 --> 00:18:47.730
You're not god, but human! And a Japanese at that!

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:51.190
I...

00:18:51.190 --> 00:18:54.320
Because you, and I...

00:18:54.320 --> 00:18:56.230
...cannot afford to die here.

00:18:57.900 --> 00:18:59.860
Lower your sword!

00:19:03.280 --> 00:19:06.950
It seems like this unidentified ship is heading towards us.

00:19:07.450 --> 00:19:10.540
A lone vessel progressing at 10 knots.

00:19:10.790 --> 00:19:12.790
I don't think it's a battleship.

00:19:12.790 --> 00:19:15.590
It must be the Executive Officer returning with the tanker!

00:19:15.590 --> 00:19:18.970
If that's him, why hasn't he radioed us yet?

00:19:18.970 --> 00:19:20.880
What if they're both captured,

00:19:20.880 --> 00:19:23.800
and this plan has already been discovered by the navy?

00:19:23.890 --> 00:19:26.010
I really hope that isn't true,

00:19:26.010 --> 00:19:29.270
but we can't omit the possibility of Lieutenant Kusaka selling us out.

00:19:29.270 --> 00:19:31.810
We must always be prepared for the worst.

00:19:32.270 --> 00:19:35.270
Time before they come within a 20 mile perimeter?

00:19:35.270 --> 00:19:37.400
In one hour's time.

00:19:37.530 --> 00:19:39.190
It's risky, but...

00:19:39.190 --> 00:19:41.740
We will act according to our agreed plan with the XO.

00:19:42.110 --> 00:19:44.530
We will send a wireless to them instead!

00:19:44.620 --> 00:19:46.240
Kadomatsu...

00:19:47.830 --> 00:19:49.540
Are you still alive, I wonder?

00:19:57.590 --> 00:20:00.170
You carry a very unique pistol.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:04.140
I'm getting more and more interested in seeing your ship.

00:20:05.640 --> 00:20:08.140
However, please do not forget this fact.

00:20:08.140 --> 00:20:11.520
At present, we are the ones who hold the authority.

00:20:11.520 --> 00:20:15.150
It is possible for me to issue an order to seize your ship.

00:20:15.150 --> 00:20:18.110
Seize our ship?! You must be joking!

00:20:18.110 --> 00:20:19.650
With this little crew?

00:20:19.820 --> 00:20:22.240
What you've seen is those on board.

00:20:22.240 --> 00:20:26.410
With my command, the navy and air force will also send troops.

00:20:27.030 --> 00:20:28.660
What?!

00:20:28.830 --> 00:20:30.330
At the Sanjaku Base,

00:20:30.330 --> 00:20:32.460
we have torpedo equipped Type One seaplanes,

00:20:32.460 --> 00:20:34.370
as well as fighter pilots.

00:20:34.670 --> 00:20:38.090
Seletar Naval Base houses the light cruiser <i>Kashii</i>,

00:20:38.090 --> 00:20:40.050
and with it, 4 destroyers.

00:20:40.800 --> 00:20:44.930
They have enough power to sink a 10,000 ton heavy class cruiser.

00:20:44.930 --> 00:20:47.300
And they've all been deployed for this operation.

00:20:48.640 --> 00:20:51.980
I want this man detained, and locked in the ship's hold.

00:20:51.980 --> 00:20:53.230
Yes!

00:20:53.310 --> 00:20:54.900
Hold on, Lieutenant Tsuda.

00:20:54.900 --> 00:20:56.150
Yes?

00:20:56.150 --> 00:20:59.320
Do not forget that he is a ranking officer.

00:20:59.570 --> 00:21:02.780
And the Commander of a mighty battleship at sea.

00:21:03.030 --> 00:21:04.450
Show him respect.

00:21:04.450 --> 00:21:06.740
Yes, I understand.

00:21:06.780 --> 00:21:09.490
Come, this way! Go down!

00:21:10.040 --> 00:21:12.700
Supplies aside, if we keep this up...

00:21:12.700 --> 00:21:16.670
it'll evolve into the worst battle between the Japanese.

00:21:21.960 --> 00:21:24.670
We're almost at Anambas, am I right?

00:21:24.930 --> 00:21:28.390
If an unidentified ship comes within 20 miles,

00:21:28.390 --> 00:21:32.310
my ship will be sending a wireless for confirmation.

00:21:32.310 --> 00:21:34.810
Lieutenant Kusaka doesn't know this, but...

00:21:35.810 --> 00:21:38.690
As a verification that I am on board the ship,

00:21:38.690 --> 00:21:41.650
I have to send a reply with a secret code we agreed upon.

00:21:41.650 --> 00:21:44.240
And I'm the only one who knows that code.

00:21:44.240 --> 00:21:46.780
What if... we don't reply?

00:21:46.820 --> 00:21:49.830
With a radar that far surpasses yours,

00:21:49.830 --> 00:21:53.830
and anti-battleship weapons of a 110,000 yard shooting range,

00:21:53.830 --> 00:21:56.500
even before your military forces start to move,

00:21:56.500 --> 00:21:58.830
they will have sunk this ship.

00:22:09.720 --> 00:22:17.240
Passing through the distant time

00:22:17.370 --> 00:22:22.440
Just peacefully

00:22:21.940 --> 00:22:34.250
Without losing your way, you walked towards me

00:22:35.390 --> 00:22:47.130
How many times have I grasped tightly those small hands of yours?

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:53.770
Not being able to do anything

00:22:54.340 --> 00:22:59.850
I kept on praying

00:23:01.210 --> 00:23:11.660
Sorrow or agony isn't enough

00:23:13.530 --> 00:23:27.340
That's why now as if I wanted to make up... I'm looking at you

00:23:40.890 --> 00:23:43.890
Is this flow of events... just as you had expected?

00:23:43.890 --> 00:23:44.930
The only thing capable of altering...

00:23:45.270 --> 00:23:47.060
...the stubborn minds of the pro-war lobbyists,

00:23:47.060 --> 00:23:48.770
is this future in front of us.

00:23:48.770 --> 00:23:50.980
Kusaka's words are just like drugs to us.

00:23:50.980 --> 00:23:52.900
They're dangerous, yet so sweet.

00:23:53.360 --> 00:23:55.940
Maybe we should be putting our strengths to better use instead.

00:23:56.400 --> 00:23:58.450
For the sake of those people who cross our paths.

00:23:58.490 --> 00:24:02.120
The operation is armed with weapons that are not meant to kill,

00:23:59.990 --> 00:24:04.960
Next Episode: Deadline

00:24:02.120 --> 00:24:04.120
but for the purpose of rescue.

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:09.960
This story is purely fiction. The names of the
characters and organizations that appear have no
connections with actual people and organizations.
